<title>USA: Continental Air flight cut short by cabin smoke.</title>
<headline>Continental Air flight cut short by cabin smoke.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Continental Airlines jet bound for Los Angeles returned to Houston 15 minutes after takeoff on Monday when the cabin filled with smoke, an airline spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>None of the 139 passengers or five crew members on the McDonnell-Douglas 80 was hurt in the incident, said Continental spokeswoman Sara Anthony.</p>
<p>Anthony said the pilot did not declare an emergency and the plane made a routine landing. &quot;It was basically nothing,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The cause of the smoke was being investigated, Anthony said.</p>
</text>
